  <!-- ========================================================================= -->
  <div class="phase-section">
    <div class="phase-banner" style="border-left-color: var(--c-blue);">
      <div class="phase-eyebrow" style="color: var(--c-blue);">PHASE 1</div>
      <div class="phase-title">Signal Ingestion &amp; Tri-Branch Front-End Bifurcation</div>
      <div class="phase-goal">GOAL: Continuously ingest live audio and mathematically bifurcate the signal into three specialized, time-aligned physical, perceptual, and raw sub-band representations.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 1 -->
    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-header">
        <div class="step-num-badge">1</div>
        <div class="step-title-block">
          <div class="step-heading">Continuous Audio Ingestion via GPU Circular Ring Buffer</div>
          <div class="step-tensor-sig">Tensor Progression: Live PCM Stream → Buffer Tensor [B=1, Channels=1, Samples=160,000]</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2col">
        <div class="content-box">
          <div class="block-label lbl-how">HOW THE INGESTION ENGINE OPERATES</div>
          <ul class="bullet-list">
            <li><strong>Memory Pre-Allocation:</strong> A fixed contiguous array of size <code>(1, 160000)</code> is initialized in GPU pinned memory, holding exactly 10.0 seconds of 16.0 kHz mono audio.</li>
            <li><strong>In-Place Rolling Shift (2.0s Stride):</strong> Every 2.0 seconds, the driver pulls the newest 32,000 samples, discards the oldest 32,000 samples via in-place tensor memory pointer shifting, and appends the new audio block.</li>
            <li><strong>80% Overlap Guarantee:</strong> Because windows overlap by 8.0 seconds, every acoustic phoneme is evaluated across multiple temporal positions within consecutive inference passes.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box">
          <div class="block-label lbl-why">FORENSIC &amp; LATENCY RATIONALE</div>
          <ul class="bullet-list">
            <li><strong>Eliminating Bus Transfer Latency:</strong> Pinned memory DMA transfers avoid CPU-GPU serialization bottlenecks, executing the full window update in <strong>&lt; 3.8 ms</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Anti-Splicing Defense:</strong> Attackers often insert brief 1.5-second cloned phrases into authentic conversations. An 80% overlap ensures a short deepfake burst is always captured in the stable center of at least one rolling window rather than on an edge boundary.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="analogy-card">
        <strong>Beginner Analogy: The Dashcam Buffer</strong>
        Think of a car dashcam that continuously keeps the last 10 minutes of driving. It doesn't record until the memory card is completely full; it constantly drops the oldest minute as a new minute arrives. This gives the AI a continuous 10-second memory horizon without ever crashing memory.
      </div>
    </div>

