  <!-- PHASE 3: CROSS-STREAM FUSION & DYNAMIC GATING -->
  <!-- ========================================================================= -->
  <div class="phase-section">
    <div class="phase-banner" style="border-left-color: var(--c-purple);">
      <div class="phase-eyebrow" style="color: var(--c-purple);">PHASE 3</div>
      <div class="phase-title">Cross-Stream Multi-Modal Fusion &amp; Dynamic Channel Gating</div>
      <div class="phase-goal">GOAL: Cross-examine physical and perceptual features via Mutual Cross-Attention and adaptively recalibrate channels under real-world attack conditions (codecs, room replay).</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 8: MCA -->
    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-header">
        <div class="step-num-badge">8</div>
        <div class="step-title-block">
          <div class="step-heading">Multi-Stream Mutual Cross-Attention (MCA) Alignment</div>
          <div class="step-tensor-sig">Symmetric Cross-Query Verification: Physical vs. Perceptual vs. Sub-Band Representations</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2col">
        <div class="content-box">
          <div class="block-label lbl-math">SYMMETRIC MCA MATHEMATICAL FORMULATION</div>
          <p style="font-size:12.5px; margin-bottom:6px;">Unlike unidirectional cross-attention, MCA enforces a bidirectional information exchange:</p>
          <div class="math-block">
            Q_{\text{lin}} = H_{\text{lin}} W_{Q1}, \quad K_{\text{mel}} = H_{\text{mel}} W_{K1}, \quad V_{\text{mel}} = H_{\text{mel}} W_{V1}<br>
            \text{Attn}_{\text{Lin}\to\text{Mel}} = \text{Softmax}\left(\frac{Q_{\text{lin}} K_{\text{mel}}^T}{\sqrt{d_k}}\right) V_{\text{mel}}
          </div>
          <div class="math-block">
            Q_{\text{mel}} = H_{\text{mel}} W_{Q2}, \quad K_{\text{lin}} = H_{\text{lin}} W_{K2}, \quad V_{\text{lin}} = H_{\text{lin}} W_{V2}<br>
            \text{Attn}_{\text{Mel}\to\text{Lin}} = \text{Softmax}\left(\frac{Q_{\text{mel}} K_{\text{lin}}^T}{\sqrt{d_k}}\right) V_{\text{lin}}
          </div>
          <div class="math-block">
            \text{Attn}_{\text{Sinc}} = \text{CrossAttend}\Big(H_{\text{sinc}}, [H_{\text{lin}} \parallel H_{\text{mel}}]\Big)
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box">
          <div class="block-label lbl-why">WHY THE DETECTIVE NEGOTIATION WORKS</div>
          <ul class="bullet-list">
            <li><strong>Cross-Domain Verification:</strong> Generative voice clones rarely fool physical and perceptual domains simultaneously.
              <br>• <em>Linear-to-Mel:</em> The Linear branch queries the Mel branch to verify if an unnatural high-frequency vocoder seam aligns with a genuine vocal tract movement.
              <br>• <em>Mel-to-Linear:</em> The Mel branch queries the Linear branch to verify if an abnormal prosodic pause is backed by physical vocoder frame-stitching artifacts.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Resolving Ambiguities:</strong> If a high-frequency spike is just microphone static, the Mel branch confirms natural vocal tract dynamics, and the model avoids a false alarm.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 9: SE Recalibration -->
    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-header">
        <div class="step-num-badge">9</div>
        <div class="step-title-block">
          <div class="step-heading">Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) Adaptive Channel Recalibration (The Fail-Safe)</div>
          <div class="step-tensor-sig">Dynamic Feature Gating: Generating Fused Latent Tensor Z ∈ [B, 1000, 256]</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2col">
        <div class="content-box">
          <div class="block-label lbl-how">SE GATING COMPUTATION</div>
          <ul class="bullet-list">
            <li>The cross-attended representations are concatenated along the channel dimension.</li>
            <li>Global average pooling calculates a channel descriptor vector $s \in \mathbb{R}^{256}$:
              <div class="math-block">s = \text{AdaptiveAvgPool}(Z_{\text{concat}})</div>
            </li>
            <li>Two fully connected layers with Sigmoid compute adaptive channel weights $g \in \mathbb{R}^{256}$:
              <div class="math-block">g = \sigma\Big(W_2 \cdot \text{GELU}(W_1 s)\Big)</div>
            </li>
            <li>Output: <span class="inline-code">Z = g ⊗ Z_concat ∈ ℝ^(B × 1000 × 256)</span>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box">
          <div class="block-label lbl-failsafe">THE REAL-WORLD FAIL-SAFE MECHANISM</div>
          <ul class="bullet-list">
            <li><strong>Replay &amp; Codec Protection:</strong> When deepfake audio travels over WhatsApp/Opus codecs or phone networks (G.711), frequencies above 4 kHz are stripped by low-pass filters. When played over a speaker, room reflections scatter physical phase.</li>
            <li><strong>Automatic Branch Switching:</strong> Under clean conditions, the SE gate balances Linear and Mel channels equally. Under heavy compression or room replay, the SE gate automatically drives linear weights to zero ($g_{\text{lin}} \to 0$) and increases Mel/prosodic weights ($g_{\text{mel}} \to 1$).</li>
            <li>The model falls back to speech rhythm and formant dynamics without manual intervention.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

